Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: nss: drop mesh "mpath not found" exception packets

ath11k_nss_mesh_obj_ext_data_callback() re-sends packets that the NSS mesh
encap returned with NSS_WIFI_MESH_ENCAP_EXT_DATA_PKT_TYPE_MPATH_NOT_FOUND_EXC
by calling eth_type_trans() and then dev_queue_xmit().  eth_type_trans()
pulls the Ethernet header, so the skb handed to mac80211 starts at the L3
header.  mac80211 then takes the first bytes of the IPv6/IPv4 header as the
destination MAC, creates bogus mesh paths (60:0x:.. for IPv6), sends PREQs
for them and asks NSS to add them, until the NSS mpath table is full and
every add fails with "failed to add an entry to mpath table".  The packet
itself is never delivered.

Keeping the Ethernet header and re-sending the packet was tried first: the
host then forwards every exception in the slow path (about 20,000 packets/s
while NSS lacked the path), and the IPQ8072A (Linksys MX5300) reset without
any kernel message in 3 of 5 runs of the test.

Drop the packet instead.  Delivery is unchanged (it was lost before as
well), and path discovery does not depend on it: NSS reports
NSS_WIFI_MESH_MSG_PATH_NOT_FOUND separately, which starts a PREQ through
ieee80211_mesh_path_offld_change_notify().

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -2055,9 +2055,17 @@
 		case NSS_WIFI_MESH_ENCAP_EXT_DATA_PKT_TYPE_MPATH_NOT_FOUND_EXC:
 			ath11k_dbg_dump(ab, ATH11K_DBG_DP_RX, "", "msdu from nss ext_data for mpath not found : ",
 					skb->data, skb->len);
-			skb->protocol = eth_type_trans(skb, dev);
-			skb_reset_network_header(skb);
-			dev_queue_xmit(skb);
+			/* Drop the packet.  Re-sending it after eth_type_trans()
+			 * hands mac80211 an skb without the Ethernet header, so the
+			 * L3 header is taken as the destination address and bogus
+			 * mesh paths (e.g. 60:0x:.. from IPv6) fill the NSS mpath
+			 * table ("failed to add an entry to mpath table").  Re-sending
+			 * it with the header kept makes the host forward every
+			 * exception in the slow path, which reset the IPQ8072A under
+			 * load.  Path discovery does not depend on this packet: NSS
+			 * reports NSS_WIFI_MESH_MSG_PATH_NOT_FOUND separately.
+			 */
+			dev_kfree_skb_any(skb);
 		break;
 		default:
 			ath11k_warn(ab, "unknown packet type received in mesh obj ext data %d",
